MUNICIPAL POLICE.
C. I. D.
Shanghai, .................................................... 192 .

INTELLIGENCE REPORT.

5. Draft of scheme for the seizure of the steamer "Ohotsk",
which states : a) Khrulinski has been intructed to establish
connections with the Cossacks engaged in painting the ship;
b) Von Berg has established connections with the "Ohotsk"
through the medium of two Tartars, one of whom is on board
and the other at Shanghai; c) Roughly 20 of the Cossack mem-
bers of the crew of the "Ohotsk" are on our side; d) List
of names Von Berg, Bielkoff, Khlebin, Drumin, Goluboff and
Lapkovski;

6. Petition dated March 13, 1926 which contains an appeal from
the crew of the "Ohotsk" to Karahan to allow them to return
to Russia in recognition for their having seized and taken
the "Ohotsk". There are no names in the space at the end
of the petition reserved for signatures;

7. Rough notes on a loose sheet of paper :
a) List of persons on board;
b) List of persons;
c) Declaration.
a) At 10 o'clock to-morrow morning;
b) Our opponents, 2600 ? 300 machine gun;
c) Hoist flag;
d) Appoint Captain;
e) Cocaine (Iv) (Khrul).

8. Soviet Consulate document dated May 22, 1925 :
Document confirming Averyanoff's request to be reinstated
as citizen of Soviet Russia;

9. Business card of Doctor B. V. Laskorousky, 58 Range Road
(Supposed to supply Goluboff with cocaine);

10. Address of one of the gang :- G. Lapkovsky, 43 Avenue du
Roi Albert, Peugeot Garage, Local.

（左侧手写批注：Copy for Mr. Sturman.）
